														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4259977">
									

<p>SCP-4730 is a long SCP with an interesting premise that, ultimately, collapses under the weight of several, minor issues. Most of them are lapses in tone which make believing that this was written by professionals difficult.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Examples</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;These&nbsp;are&nbsp;not&nbsp;all,&nbsp;just&nbsp;some</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>All containment areas at Site-70 are to be kept at least 300 meters away from any door requiring level 4 or higher security clearance and have at least one 50&#160;cm thick steel wall obstructing direct line of sight between them.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>These exact numbers, 300 meters, 50&#160;cm, never appear again. They are arbitary. If a wall is 299 meters away from a door does containment fail automatically? No. It's the X by X by X containment cell issue but in a different format.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A MTF Nu-7 battery of at least 120 members are to remained stationed at Site-70 in compliment to its standing armed guard force of 1000.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Again why is 120 the magic number? Furthermore, anyone reading this wont know what's contained (because that's blacked out below), but will know exactly how many armed guards are on site by default: vital intel for most saboteurs.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4730 is an anomaly that affects a randomly chosen level 4 or higher security card at Site-70 every 2 to 40 days and activates upon use on a level 4 door.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So there are leveled cards AND doors? If containment is an issue&#8230;then why keep using the system that causes issues? Why not use that MTF battery to screen clearance levels in different ways? Why not find an alternative method to the card+door system that causes hostiles with gauss weaponry to invade?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4730-3 instance covers Researcher Mochizuka's mouth with their hand. Researcher Mochizuka is escorted through various corridors before being deposited in a stark white interrogation room marked 75T. Mochizuka is handcuffed to a metal chair in front of a metallic table and left alone for two minutes and 20 seconds before someone enters the room and sits across the table from Mochizuka. Person is of masculine appearance and designated as Interviewer.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This doesn't read as clinical, official notes. This reads as pure narrative description, as though from a novel. The room isn't white it's 'stark white.' Why do we need to know that the interviewer is of 'masculine appearance' or that the furniture is 'metallic?'</p>
<blockquote>
<p>You better damn be, I do NOT enjoy being woken up by a guard ordering me to my computer with no clue as to why.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The dialogue suffers as well. This doesn't sound like one of the people responsible for managing global Foundation operations, this sounds like an unprofessional kid who's never experienced a sudden emergency or meeting before, which is impossible considering Foundation operations in general.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>The concept is promising. The execution was not, unfortunately.</p>

							</div>

								
					
