<p>Roger that, I'll give it an edit tonight and tomorrow to make it have a more consistent clinical tone. See below for responses to your examples.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I wanted to avoid being vague in the containment procedures. The point of the distance and wall is to make the invading force have to slog through defenders and not immediately pop up in a containment area. I suppose I could replace that with &quot;Containment areas are to be kept a defensible distance away from any level 4 door per Site-70 Nu-7 commander discretion&quot; or something. Same goes for the battery of 120.</p>
<p>I do novel writing as a hobby so breaking that is a bit hard. I will remove extraneous details.</p>
<p>As for why they keep using the level 4 card+door system? The invading forces can actually use whatever door with whatever security clearance they want. Site-70 is constructed around a disinformation campaign to make everyone but the O5s and site command think it is of vital importance. This is to convince the alternate foundation that they don't need to appear anywhere else besides level 4 doors at site 70.</p>
<p>Is there anything I can do to make that a bit more apparent?</p>
</div>
