														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4260394">
									

<p>Sorry, this is a downvote for me. It was a neutral vote awaiting some improvements, but it seemed to get worse the further I went.</p>
<p>First, I would remove the second picture entirely. It in no way looks like footage from a security camera. It's also clearly a picture of a US military exercise, using equipment that would clearly be outdated considering the nature of the -3 MTF instance.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The method of accessing our universe makes no sense. If they've done this dozens of realities, why is it that they can only enter ours through a randomly selected level 4 or higher keycard at one site? That seems a pretty poor and uncontrollable method of entry.</p>
<p>The properties of the Gauss rifles are never explained, but I'm not sure you have your principles correct. Popular conception of a Gauss rifle has a lightweight piece of metal accelerated to high speed. Conventionally this would mean that there is no such thing as a &quot;high caliber&quot; Gauss rifle as the projectiles are typically theorized to be several factors smaller than modern rifle projectiles.</p>
<p>I really didn't like that I felt like 4730-3 could have been replaced with Fallout's Brotherhood of Steel seamlessly.</p>
<p>There were many elements that were thrown in out of nowhere that were disorienting. I have no idea what was going on with the giant crosses. The evil space baddies mining everybody's reality for resources is very cliche.</p>
<p>The whole lot with the captured researcher was bewildering to me and I don't know what I was meant to get out of it. I'm also skeptical of the preservation of all of this conveniently important dialog over a video stream that is sending data to a different reality.</p>
<p>The -3 interviewed can't decide if he's a member of a supreme reality, a thoughtless bruiser for hire, or an imbecile who doesn't understand the most basic functioning of the organization he works for and proclaims dimensionally superior.</p>
<p>The portrayal of the O5 council largely felt like a throwaway gag with little to no thought into how members in that position would react or even much research into their communication in other well established tales.</p>
<p>I like the idea of a decoy site containing an anomalous entity that attacks it for the purpose of securing the SCPs. I absolutely hate the method (since when is blowing things up containment? Why does this nearly omniscient Foundation only enter one site at specified doors? Etc.)</p>
<p>I do like the idea of a competing Foundation reality that has antagonistic goals to ours and is possibly under the persuasion or a power they themselves don't understand.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
<em>As a courtesy to our readers on mobile devices, please collapse long posts. ~Zyn</em>
<p>I think this SCP is all over the place. My downvote is in hopes of it being removed and going back to the drafts forum where I think it should have spent more time and far more criticism.</p>
<p>If you're attached to this universe, my suggestion is to strip away all of the logs and spend some time picking it apart. Write it as an SCP and leave out the section that's trying to be a tale. Put your work into establishing your baseline, create a really solid foundation (pun intended) and create it as an SCP. If that's accepted by the community, that's when I would begin trying to expand the story via tales</p>
<p>I also saw at least one instance of SCP-XXXX-3 that should be replaced.</p>

							</div>

								
